exec(open('/home/claude/work/gita/gc.py').read())
V=[
X(1,'THE MOST SECRET KNOWLEDGE',
 S('Krishna leaning close to share a secret with Arjuna','KA','light','GUHYATAMAM'),
 'The Lord said: To you, who do not find fault, I will now declare this most secret knowledge together with realisation; knowing it, you will be freed from evil.',
 [('idam tu te guhyatamam','<b>this most secret, to you</b>'),('pravakṣyāmi anasūyave','<b>I will declare, to one who does not carp</b>'),('jñānam vijñāna-sahitam','<b>knowledge with realisation</b>'),('yat jñātvā mokṣyase aśubhāt','<b>knowing which you will be freed from ill</b>')],
 'Chapter 9 opens with Kṛṣṇa calling this the most secret knowledge.',
 'Arjuna is called <i>anasūyu</i>, one without envy or fault-finding: the right listener. Commentators say the “secret” is the intimacy of devotion, revealed only to the open-hearted.',
 'Openness is the key that opens deep teaching. Come without suspicion.',
 'The <b>most secret knowledge</b>.'),
X(2,'THE ROYAL SECRET',
 S('A crown-shaped light, easy to reach','','crown','RĀJA-VIDYĀ'),
 '“This is the king of sciences, the king of secrets, the supreme purifier, directly experienced, in keeping with dharma, very easy to practise, and imperishable.”',
 [('rāja-vidyā rāja-guhyam','<b>king of sciences, king of secrets</b>'),('pavitram idam uttamam','<b>this supreme purifier</b>'),('pratyakṣa-avagamam','<b>directly experienced</b>'),('dharmyam su-sukham kartum','<b>righteous, very easy to practise</b>'),('avyayam','<b>imperishable</b>')],
 'Kṛṣṇa praises this teaching with seven qualities.',
 'Note <i>pratyakṣa</i>, directly experienced, and <i>susukha</i>, easy to practise: devotion is not remote theory. The chapter’s name, Rāja Vidyā Rāja Guhya Yoga, comes from this verse.',
 'The highest teaching is also simple to practise. Don’t assume depth means difficulty.',
 'The royal secret is <b>easy and direct</b>.'),
X(3,'THOSE WITHOUT FAITH',
 S('People turning away from a light, walking a circle of death','','wheel','NO FAITH'),
 '“People who have no faith in this dharma, scorcher of foes, do not reach me and return to the path of death and rebirth.”',
 [('aśraddadhānāḥ puruṣāḥ','<b>people without faith</b>'),('dharmasya asya parantapa','<b>in this dharma</b>'),('aprāpya mām nivartante','<b>not reaching me, they return</b>'),('mṛtyu-saṃsāra-vartmani','<b>to the path of death and rebirth</b>')],
 'Without faith, one stays in the cycle.',
 'Faith (<i>śraddhā</i>) opens the door; its absence keeps it shut. Commentators say faith here means willingness to try.',
 'A little trust opens many doors.',
 'Without faith, <b>the cycle continues</b>.'),
X(4,'PERVADING ALL, YET UNSEEN',
 S('An unseen presence holding many beings','K','cosmic','AVYAKTA-MŪRTI'),
 '“By me, in my unmanifest form, this whole world is pervaded. All beings dwell in me, but I do not dwell in them.”',
 [('mayā tatam idam sarvam','<b>by me all this is pervaded</b>'),('jagat avyakta-mūrtinā','<b>the world, by my unmanifest form</b>'),('mat-sthāni sarva-bhūtāni','<b>all beings dwell in me</b>'),('na ca aham teṣu avasthitaḥ','<b>but I do not dwell in them</b>')],
 'A paradox: God pervades all, yet is not contained by anything.',
 'Commentators compare it to space: everything is in space, yet space is not limited by the things in it. The next verse deepens the paradox.',
 'The Divine supports everything and is limited by nothing.',
 'All in me; <b>I not in them</b>.'),
X(5,'MY DIVINE YOGA',
 S('Krishna smiling at a riddle, beings floating in a vast light','K','star','SEE MY YOGA!'),
 '“And yet beings do not dwell in me: see my divine yoga! Sustaining beings, yet not dwelling in them, my Self is the source of beings.”',
 [('na ca mat-sthāni bhūtāni','<b>and yet beings do not dwell in me</b>'),('paśya me yogam aiśvaram','<b>see my divine yoga</b>'),('bhūta-bhṛt na ca bhūta-sthaḥ','<b>sustaining beings, not dwelling in them</b>'),('mama ātmā bhūta-bhāvanaḥ','<b>my Self is the source of beings</b>')],
 'The paradox goes further: beings are not even in him.',
 'Śaṅkara reads it as: beings only appear in God, as a snake appears in a rope; ultimately only God is. Rāmānuja reads: beings depend on him without touching his nature. Kṛṣṇa calls it his divine mystery.',
 'Some truths are mysteries to be wondered at, not solved.',
 '<b>See my divine yoga!</b>'),
X(6,'LIKE WIND IN SPACE',
 S('Wind moving everywhere within open sky','','storm','ĀKĀŚA'),
 '“As the mighty wind, moving everywhere, always rests in space, so know that all beings rest in me.”',
 [('yathā ākāśa-sthitaḥ nityam','<b>as, always resting in space</b>'),('vāyuḥ sarvatra-gaḥ mahān','<b>the mighty wind moving everywhere</b>'),('tathā sarvāṇi bhūtāni','<b>so all beings</b>'),('mat-sthāni iti upadhāraya','<b>rest in me, understand</b>')],
 'An image for the paradox: wind in space.',
 'Wind is in space, moves freely, yet does not touch or change space. So beings move in God without affecting him.',
 'However stormy life is, it moves in a vast stillness.',
 'Like wind <b>resting in space</b>.'),
X(7,'THE KALPA ENDS AND BEGINS',
 S('Beings dissolving into Krishna and emerging again','K','wheel','KALPA'),
 '“At the end of a kalpa, son of Kuntī, all beings enter my nature; at the beginning of a kalpa, I send them forth again.”',
 [('sarva-bhūtāni kaunteya','<b>all beings</b>'),('prakṛtim yānti māmikām','<b>enter my nature</b>'),('kalpa-kṣaye','<b>at the end of a kalpa</b>'),('punaḥ tāni kalpa-ādau','<b>again, at the start of a kalpa</b>'),('visṛjāmi aham','<b>I send them forth</b>')],
 'Cosmic cycles of dissolution and creation.',
 'This continues 8.18–19. Commentators: creation is the Lord’s ongoing activity, through his nature.',
 'Endings and beginnings are part of one great rhythm.',
 'All return to me, <b>and come forth again</b>.'),
X(8,'THROUGH MY NATURE',
 S('Krishna directing nature as a potter shapes clay','K','seed','AVAŚA'),
 '“Resting on my own nature, I send forth again and again this whole host of beings, helpless under the sway of nature.”',
 [('prakṛtim svām avaṣṭabhya','<b>resting on my own nature</b>'),('visṛjāmi punaḥ punaḥ','<b>I send forth again and again</b>'),('bhūta-grāmam imam kṛtsnam','<b>this whole host of beings</b>'),('avaśam prakṛteḥ vaśāt','<b>helpless under nature’s sway</b>')],
 'God creates through nature; beings are carried by their nature.',
 'Commentators: beings are helpless because bound by karma and guṇas; God acts freely through prakṛti.',
 'We are carried by habits until we find freedom.',
 'Created again <b>and again</b>.'),
X(9,'UNBOUND BY CREATION',
 S('Krishna sitting calmly, detached, while worlds turn','K','wheel','UDĀSĪNA'),
 '“These actions do not bind me, Dhanañjaya, for I sit as one indifferent, unattached to these actions.”',
 [('na ca mām tāni karmāṇi','<b>and those actions do not me</b>'),('nibadhnanti dhanañjaya','<b>bind</b>'),('udāsīna-vat āsīnam','<b>sitting as if indifferent</b>'),('asaktam teṣu karmasu','<b>unattached to those actions</b>')],
 'Even creating worlds does not bind God.',
 '<i>Udāsīna</i>, sitting above, like a neutral witness. Commentators say this models detached action for us too.',
 'Act fully; stay unattached. Even God works this way.',
 'Creating worlds, <b>yet unbound</b>.'),
X(10,'NATURE PRODUCES, I WATCH',
 S('Nature turning a wheel while Krishna watches','K','light','ADHYAKṢA'),
 '“Under my supervision nature produces the moving and the unmoving. Because of this, son of Kuntī, the world revolves.”',
 [('mayā adhyakṣeṇa prakṛtiḥ','<b>with me as overseer, nature</b>'),('sūyate sa-cara-acaram','<b>produces moving and unmoving</b>'),('hetunā anena kaunteya','<b>for this reason</b>'),('jagat viparivartate','<b>the world revolves</b>')],
 'God as overseer; nature as producer.',
 '<i>Adhyakṣa</i>, presiding witness. Commentators compare it to the sun, in whose presence life grows without the sun “doing” it.',
 'Presence itself can be powerful. Calm presence changes a room.',
 'In my presence, <b>nature creates</b>.'),
X(11,'THEY SEE ONLY THE HUMAN FORM',
 S('People laughing at a human-looking Krishna, unaware of his glory','K','light','MĀNUṢĪM TANUM'),
 '“The deluded scorn me when I take a human form, not knowing my higher nature as the great Lord of beings.”',
 [('avajānanti mām mūḍhāḥ','<b>the deluded scorn me</b>'),('mānuṣīm tanum āśritam','<b>having taken a human body</b>'),('param bhāvam ajānantaḥ','<b>not knowing my higher nature</b>'),('mama bhūta-maheśvaram','<b>as great Lord of beings</b>')],
 'Many see only a man in Kṛṣṇa.',
 'Compare 7.24. Commentators recall people in the epic who scorned Kṛṣṇa, like Śiśupāla and Duryodhana.',
 'The Divine often comes in humble form. Look closely.',
 'Scorned <b>in human form</b>.'),
X(12,'VAIN HOPES',
 S('People with empty hopes, a dark nature clouding them','','demon','MOGHA'),
 '“Of vain hopes, vain actions, vain knowledge, and confused minds, they take on the deceptive nature of rākṣasas and asuras.”',
 [('mogha-āśāḥ mogha-karmāṇaḥ','<b>of vain hopes, vain actions</b>'),('mogha-jñānāḥ vicetasaḥ','<b>vain knowledge, senseless</b>'),('rākṣasīm āsurīm ca eva','<b>rākṣasa and asura</b>'),('prakṛtim mohinīm śritāḥ','<b>deluding nature they take on</b>')],
 'Those who scorn the Divine live in futility.',
 'Commentators say <i>mogha</i>, futile, describes hopes and acts cut off from their source. Chapter 16 develops this nature.',
 'Hopes without a deeper root often end in disappointment.',
 'Hopes <b>without a root are vain</b>.'),
X(13,'THE GREAT SOULS',
 S('Great souls worshipping with single-minded love','KA','heart','MAHĀTMĀNAḤ'),
 '“But the great souls, Pārtha, sheltered in my divine nature, worship me with undivided mind, knowing me as the imperishable source of beings.”',
 [('mahā-ātmānaḥ tu mām pārtha','<b>but the great souls, me</b>'),('daivīm prakṛtim āśritāḥ','<b>sheltered in divine nature</b>'),('bhajanti ananya-manasaḥ','<b>worship with undivided mind</b>'),('jñātvā bhūta-ādim avyayam','<b>knowing me as source of beings, imperishable</b>')],
 'In contrast: the great souls who worship.',
 '<i>Mahātmā</i>, great soul, is defined by devotion. The “divine nature” is described in 16.1–3.',
 'Greatness of soul shows in love, not in power.',
 'Great souls <b>worship with one mind</b>.'),
X(14,'ALWAYS SINGING',
 S('Devotees singing and bowing, firm in vows','P','heart','KĪRTAN'),
 '“Always singing my praises, striving with firm vows, bowing to me with devotion, ever united, they worship me.”',
 [('satatam kīrtayantaḥ mām','<b>always singing of me</b>'),('yatantaḥ ca dṛḍha-vratāḥ','<b>striving, firm in vows</b>'),('namasyantaḥ ca mām bhaktyā','<b>bowing to me with devotion</b>'),('nitya-yuktāḥ upāsate','<b>ever united, they worship</b>')],
 'Ways of devotion: singing, effort, bowing.',
 'This verse inspired the <i>kīrtan</i> and <i>bhajan</i> traditions. Commentators list the three: speech (singing), effort (vows), body (bowing).',
 'Sing, strive, bow: devotion uses voice, will and body.',
 'Singing, striving, <b>bowing</b>.'),
X(15,'MANY WAYS OF WORSHIP',
 S('Some worship the One, some the many, some all as God','P','light','EKATVA · PṚTHAKTVA'),
 '“Others too worship me by the sacrifice of knowledge: as the One, as distinct, as manifold, facing every direction.”',
 [('jñāna-yajñena ca api anye','<b>others by the sacrifice of knowledge</b>'),('yajantaḥ mām upāsate','<b>sacrificing, worship me</b>'),('ekatvena pṛthaktvena','<b>as one, as distinct</b>'),('bahudhā viśvato-mukham','<b>as manifold, facing everywhere</b>')],
 'Different ways of seeing God, all valid.',
 'Commentators read three views: non-dual (one), dual (distinct), and seeing God in many forms. The Gītā includes all.',
 'There is room for many ways of seeing the Divine.',
 'As one, as many: <b>all worship me</b>.'),
X(16,'I AM THE RITUAL',
 S('Every part of a sacred fire ritual glowing with Krishna’s light','','fire','AHAM KRATUḤ'),
 '“I am the ritual, I am the sacrifice, I am the offering to ancestors, I am the healing herb; I am the mantra, I am the ghee, I am the fire, I am the oblation.”',
 [('aham kratuḥ aham yajñaḥ','<b>I am the rite, I am the sacrifice</b>'),('svadhā aham','<b>I am the ancestral offering</b>'),('aham auṣadham','<b>I am the healing herb</b>'),('mantraḥ aham aham eva ājyam','<b>I am mantra, ghee</b>'),('aham agniḥ aham hutam','<b>I am fire, the offering</b>')],
 'Every element of worship is God.',
 'This recalls 4.24 (brahmārpaṇam). Commentators note <i>auṣadha</i>, herb or medicine: healing too is divine.',
 'Every part of a good act, tools, words, gift, can be seen as sacred.',
 'I am <b>every part of the offering</b>.'),
X(17,'FATHER, MOTHER, SUPPORT',
 S('Krishna as father, mother and grandfather of the world','K','family','PITĀ · MĀTĀ'),
 '“I am the father of this world, the mother, the supporter, the grandsire; the knowable, the purifier, the syllable Oṃ, and the Ṛg, Sāma and Yajur Vedas.”',
 [('pitā aham asya jagataḥ','<b>I am the father of this world</b>'),('mātā dhātā pitāmahaḥ','<b>mother, supporter, grandsire</b>'),('vedyam pavitram oṃkāraḥ','<b>the knowable, purifier, Oṃ</b>'),('ṛk sāma yajuḥ eva ca','<b>Ṛk, Sāma and Yajus</b>')],
 'God as every relationship: father, mother, grandparent.',
 'A tender verse. Commentators note God is both mother and father, the whole of family love, and all scripture.',
 'Whatever love you seek in a parent, the Divine holds in full.',
 'Father, mother, <b>all in one</b>.'),
X(18,'THE GOAL AND THE FRIEND',
 S('Krishna as home, refuge, friend, the goal at the end of a path','K','heart','SUHṚT'),
 '“I am the goal, the supporter, the Lord, the witness, the home, the refuge, the friend; the origin and dissolution, the ground, the treasure-house and the imperishable seed.”',
 [('gatiḥ bhartā prabhuḥ sākṣī','<b>goal, supporter, Lord, witness</b>'),('nivāsaḥ śaraṇam suhṛt','<b>home, refuge, friend</b>'),('prabhavaḥ pralayaḥ sthānam','<b>origin, dissolution, ground</b>'),('nidhānam bījam avyayam','<b>treasure-house, imperishable seed</b>')],
 'A list of the Lord’s relationships to us.',
 'Twelve names in two lines. Commentators love <i>śaraṇam suhṛt</i>, refuge and friend. Many recite this verse in prayer.',
 'God is home, refuge and friend. You are never homeless.',
 'Home, refuge, <b>friend</b>.'),
X(19,'HEAT AND RAIN',
 S('Krishna as sun giving heat and sending rain','K','sun','SAT · ASAT'),
 '“I give heat; I hold back and send forth the rain. I am immortality and also death; being and non-being, Arjuna.”',
 [('tapāmi aham','<b>I give heat</b>'),('aham varṣam nigṛhṇāmi utsṛjāmi ca','<b>I withhold and send rain</b>'),('amṛtam ca eva mṛtyuḥ ca','<b>immortality and death</b>'),('sat asat ca aham arjuna','<b>being and non-being am I</b>')],
 'God in nature’s forces, life and death alike.',
 'Commentators note the Gītā does not hide that death too is in God. Everything, pleasant and unpleasant, has the same source.',
 'Both the gifts and the losses of life come from one source.',
 'Life and death <b>alike are mine</b>.'),
X(20,'RITUALISTS SEEKING HEAVEN',
 S('Ritualists drinking soma, rising to Indra’s heaven','','gods','SVARGA'),
 '“Knowers of the three Vedas, drinking soma, purified of sin, worship me with sacrifices and pray for the way to heaven. Reaching the holy world of Indra, they enjoy the divine pleasures of the gods.”',
 [('trai-vidyāḥ mām soma-pāḥ','<b>knowers of three Vedas, soma-drinkers</b>'),('yajñaiḥ iṣṭvā svar-gatim prārthayante','<b>worshipping by sacrifice, pray for heaven</b>'),('te puṇyam āsādya surendra-lokam','<b>reaching the holy world of Indra</b>'),('aśnanti divyān divi deva-bhogān','<b>enjoy divine pleasures in heaven</b>')],
 'Ritualists who seek heaven get it.',
 'Note: they worship Kṛṣṇa (“me”) without knowing it. Commentators: their reward is real but temporary, as the next verse shows.',
 'Good deeds bring good results. The Gītā asks: is that all you want?',
 'Ritual <b>earns heaven</b>.'),
X(21,'AND THEN THEY RETURN',
 S('People descending from heaven back to earth','','wheel','GATA-ĀGATAM'),
 '“Having enjoyed that vast heaven, their merit spent, they enter the world of mortals. Thus, following the three Vedas for desires, they come and go.”',
 [('te tam bhuktvā svarga-lokam viśālam','<b>having enjoyed that vast heaven</b>'),('kṣīṇe puṇye martya-lokam viśanti','<b>merit spent, they enter the mortal world</b>'),('evam trayī-dharmam anuprapannāḥ','<b>thus following the Vedic dharma</b>'),('gata-āgatam kāma-kāmāḥ labhante','<b>desirers of desires get coming and going</b>')],
 'Heaven ends when merit runs out.',
 'Like a bank balance spent. Commentators say this is why the Gītā points beyond heaven.',
 'Rewards run out. Seek what doesn’t.',
 'Merit spent, <b>they return</b>.'),
X(22,'I CARRY WHAT THEY NEED',
 S('Krishna carrying a load of supplies for devotees','K','gift','YOGA-KṢEMAM'),
 '“But to those who worship me alone, thinking of no other, ever united with me, I bring what they lack and preserve what they have.”',
 [('ananyāḥ cintayantaḥ mām','<b>thinking of me, with no other</b>'),('ye janāḥ paryupāsate','<b>the people who worship</b>'),('teṣām nitya-abhiyuktānām','<b>of those ever united</b>'),('yoga-kṣemam vahāmi aham','<b>I carry their getting and keeping</b>')],
 'One of the most beloved promises in the Gītā.',
 '<i>Yoga-kṣema</i>, getting what one lacks and keeping what one has, is the motto of India’s Life Insurance Corporation. Commentators note the image of God personally carrying the devotee’s burden. Compare 2.45, where yoga-kṣema anxiety is to be given up.',
 'Trust the Divine to carry what you need. It frees your mind for love.',
 '<b>I carry their needs</b>.'),
X(23,'OTHER GODS WORSHIP ME',
 S('Worshippers at other shrines whose offerings flow to Krishna','','gods','TO ME'),
 '“Even those devotees who worship other gods with faith, son of Kuntī, worship me alone, though not by the proper way.”',
 [('ye api anya-devatā-bhaktāḥ','<b>even devotees of other gods</b>'),('yajante śraddhayā anvitāḥ','<b>worshipping with faith</b>'),('te api mām eva kaunteya','<b>they too, me alone</b>'),('yajanti avidhi-pūrvakam','<b>worship, though not by the proper way</b>')],
 'All sincere worship reaches the one God.',
 'A generous verse, with a qualifier: “not by the proper way” means without knowing the true object. Commentators debate how much this embraces other traditions.',
 'Sincere worship anywhere reaches the Highest.',
 'All worship <b>reaches me</b>.'),
X(24,'THE ENJOYER OF ALL SACRIFICES',
 S('Krishna receiving all offerings; some people not recognising him and falling','K','fire','BHOKTĀ'),
 '“For I am the enjoyer and Lord of all sacrifices. But they do not know me in truth, and so they fall.”',
 [('aham hi sarva-yajñānām','<b>for I, of all sacrifices</b>'),('bhoktā ca prabhuḥ eva ca','<b>am the enjoyer and Lord</b>'),('na tu mām abhijānanti','<b>but they do not know me</b>'),('tattvena ataḥ cyavanti te','<b>in truth, so they fall</b>')],
 'Not knowing who receives the offering limits its fruit.',
 'Commentators: knowing the true recipient turns worship into a path to freedom.',
 'Know whom you are offering to. It changes the offering.',
 'I receive <b>all offerings</b>.'),
X(25,'YOU BECOME WHAT YOU WORSHIP',
 S('Four paths leading to gods, ancestors, spirits, and Krishna','','gods','YĀNTI'),
 '“Worshippers of the gods go to the gods; worshippers of ancestors go to the ancestors; worshippers of spirits go to the spirits; and my worshippers come to me.”',
 [('yānti deva-vratāḥ devān','<b>god-worshippers go to gods</b>'),('pitṝn yānti pitṛ-vratāḥ','<b>ancestor-worshippers to ancestors</b>'),('bhūtāni yānti bhūta-ijyāḥ','<b>spirit-worshippers to spirits</b>'),('yānti mat-yājinaḥ api mām','<b>my worshippers come to me</b>')],
 'We reach what we worship.',
 'A simple law: the object of devotion shapes the destination. Commentators link it to 8.6.',
 'What you give your heart to, you move toward.',
 'You reach <b>what you worship</b>.'),
X(26,'A LEAF, A FLOWER, A FRUIT',
 S('A devotee offering a leaf, a flower, a fruit and a little water to Krishna','KA','lotus','PATRAM PUṢPAM'),
 '“Whoever offers me with devotion a leaf, a flower, a fruit or water, that offering of love from the pure-hearted I accept.”',
 [('patram puṣpam phalam toyam','<b>a leaf, a flower, a fruit, water</b>'),('yaḥ me bhaktyā prayacchati','<b>who offers me with devotion</b>'),('tat aham bhakti-upahṛtam','<b>that offering of devotion I</b>'),('aśnāmi prayata-ātmanaḥ','<b>accept, from the pure-hearted</b>')],
 'Perhaps the most loved verse of devotion.',
 'The simplest offerings, anyone can afford. Commentators tell stories: Vidura’s wife feeding Kṛṣṇa banana peels in her love, Sudāmā’s handful of rice. What matters is the love, not the gift.',
 'You don’t need wealth to worship. A leaf with love is enough.',
 'A leaf, a flower, <b>with love</b>.',
 ("Just a leaf?","A leaf, with love, is accepted. A palace without love is not.")),
X(27,'OFFER EVERYTHING',
 S('A person doing daily things, each one placed as an offering','P','gift','MAD-ARPAṆAM'),
 '“Whatever you do, whatever you eat, whatever you offer, whatever you give, whatever austerity you practise, son of Kuntī, do it as an offering to me.”',
 [('yat karoṣi yat aśnāsi','<b>whatever you do, whatever you eat</b>'),('yat juhoṣi dadāsi yat','<b>whatever you offer, whatever you give</b>'),('yat tapasyasi kaunteya','<b>whatever austerity you do</b>'),('tat kuruṣva mat-arpaṇam','<b>do it as an offering to me</b>')],
 'Turn all of life into offering.',
 'Commentators say this is the simplest complete practice: every act, eating included, becomes worship. It joins karma yoga and bhakti.',
 'Before eating or working, offer it. That small habit transforms the day.',
 'Do everything <b>as an offering</b>.'),
X(28,'FREED FROM THE BONDS',
 S('Chains of good and bad results falling away','Y','chain','FREE'),
 '“Thus you will be freed from the bonds of action, with their good and bad fruits. With your self united in this yoga of renunciation, freed, you will come to me.”',
 [('śubha-aśubha-phalaiḥ evam','<b>thus from good and bad fruits</b>'),('mokṣyase karma-bandhanaiḥ','<b>you will be freed from bonds of action</b>'),('sannyāsa-yoga-yukta-ātmā','<b>self joined in the yoga of renunciation</b>'),('vimuktaḥ mām upaiṣyasi','<b>freed, you will come to me</b>')],
 'Offering everything frees from karma.',
 'Commentators: offering is renunciation in practice. You give up ownership of the fruit by giving it to God.',
 'Offer the result, and its weight lifts.',
 'Offering everything <b>frees you</b>.'),
X(29,'THE SAME TO ALL',
 S('Krishna the same to all, devotees close in his heart','K','heart','SAMAḤ'),
 '“I am the same to all beings; to me none is hateful, none dear. But those who worship me with devotion are in me, and I am in them.”',
 [('samaḥ aham sarva-bhūteṣu','<b>I am the same to all beings</b>'),('na me dveṣyaḥ asti na priyaḥ','<b>none is hateful or dear to me</b>'),('ye bhajanti tu mām bhaktyā','<b>but those who worship me with devotion</b>'),('mayi te teṣu ca api aham','<b>they are in me, and I in them</b>')],
 'God loves equally, yet the devoted feel his closeness.',
 'Commentators compare it to the sun: it shines on all, but only those who open the window feel its warmth. Not favouritism, but openness.',
 'The Divine is equally near to all. Devotion opens the window.',
 'Same to all; <b>close to the devoted</b>.'),
X(30,'EVEN THE WORST',
 S('A person with a dark past turning toward Krishna with devotion','P','light','SĀDHUḤ EVA'),
 '“Even if a very wicked person worships me with undivided devotion, he should be considered good, for he has rightly resolved.”',
 [('api cet su-durācāraḥ','<b>even if very ill-behaved</b>'),('bhajate mām ananya-bhāk','<b>worships me with undivided devotion</b>'),('sādhuḥ eva saḥ mantavyaḥ','<b>he should be thought good</b>'),('samyak vyavasitaḥ hi saḥ','<b>for he has rightly resolved</b>')],
 'Hope for anyone: sincere turning makes one good.',
 'Commentators: the resolve itself marks the beginning of goodness. Stories like Vālmīki, once a robber, are cited.',
 'It is never too late to turn toward the good.',
 'Even the worst <b>who turn are good</b>.'),
X(31,'MY DEVOTEE NEVER PERISHES',
 S('Krishna declaring a promise, a devotee safe','K','heart','NA PRAṆAŚYATI'),
 '“He soon becomes righteous and attains lasting peace. Son of Kuntī, declare it boldly: my devotee never perishes.”',
 [('kṣipram bhavati dharma-ātmā','<b>soon becomes righteous</b>'),('śaśvat-śāntim nigacchati','<b>attains lasting peace</b>'),('kaunteya pratijānīhi','<b>declare it boldly</b>'),('na me bhaktaḥ praṇaśyati','<b>my devotee never perishes</b>')],
 'A famous promise: my devotee never perishes.',
 'Kṛṣṇa asks Arjuna to declare it, perhaps because a devotee’s word carries weight. Commentators treasure this as a guarantee.',
 'Devotion is a safe path. Walk it without fear.',
 '<b>My devotee never perishes</b>.'),
X(32,'OPEN TO ALL',
 S('People of all walks of life walking toward Krishna','K','family','ALL ARE WELCOME'),
 '“For those who take refuge in me, Pārtha, even those of humble birth, women, vaiśyas and śūdras too, reach the supreme goal.”',
 [('mām hi pārtha vyapāśritya','<b>taking refuge in me</b>'),('ye api syuḥ pāpa-yonayaḥ','<b>even those of lowly birth</b>'),('striyaḥ vaiśyāḥ tathā śūdrāḥ','<b>women, vaiśyas and śūdras</b>'),('te api yānti parām gatim','<b>they too reach the supreme goal</b>')],
 'Devotion is open to everyone.',
 'In its time this was radical: those often excluded from Vedic study are welcomed to the highest goal. Modern readers may wince at the phrasing, which reflects ancient social views; the teaching itself is inclusion. Commentators differ on how to read “pāpa-yoni”.',
 'No one is shut out from the Divine. That is the heart of this verse.',
 'The highest goal <b>is open to all</b>.'),
X(33,'HOW MUCH MORE THE HOLY',
 S('Sages and kings bowing, a passing world behind','','sage','MĀM BHAJASVA'),
 '“How much more, then, holy Brahmins and devoted royal sages! Having come into this impermanent, joyless world, worship me.”',
 [('kim punaḥ brāhmaṇāḥ puṇyāḥ','<b>how much more holy Brahmins</b>'),('bhaktāḥ rāja-ṛṣayaḥ tathā','<b>and devoted royal sages</b>'),('anityam asukham lokam','<b>this impermanent, joyless world</b>'),('imam prāpya bhajasva mām','<b>having come into it, worship me</b>')],
 'If all can reach him, how much more those already devoted.',
 '<i>Anityam asukham</i>: impermanent, without lasting joy. Commentators say this is not pessimism but realism, turning us toward lasting joy.',
 'This life passes. Use it for what lasts.',
 'In a passing world, <b>worship me</b>.'),
X(34,'MIND ON ME',
 S('Arjuna with mind, love, worship and bowing all directed to Krishna','KA','heart','MAN-MANĀ BHAVA'),
 '“Fix your mind on me, be devoted to me, worship me, bow to me. Thus united, with me as your goal, you will come to me.”',
 [('mat-manāḥ bhava','<b>fix your mind on me</b>'),('mat-bhaktaḥ','<b>be devoted to me</b>'),('mat-yājī','<b>worship me</b>'),('mām namaskuru','<b>bow to me</b>'),('mām eva eṣyasi','<b>you will come to me</b>')],
 'The chapter ends with the four-fold call of devotion.',
 'This verse returns almost word for word as 18.65, near the Gītā’s end. Commentators see it as the essence of bhakti: mind, heart, action and body all turned to God.',
 'Mind, love, action, body: turn all four toward the Highest.',
 '<b>Man-manā bhava</b>: mind on me.'),
]
